{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1554924-how-would-the-different-types-of-wyrm-taint-smell","id":1554924,"title":"How would the different types of Wyrm-taint smell?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-01T19:19:59-07:00","id":1554924,"title":"How would the different types of Wyrm-taint smell?","content":"I remember reading in the Book of the Wyrm that as a storyteller you can give different aspects of the Wyrm different scents. So I wonder what the taint of each Urge-Wyrm could smell like. Maybe Wyrm-taint associated with Cruelty could smell like sweat, Violence could smell like blood, Consumption could smell of death, Smoke could smell like a sickly sweet smoke, Hellfire could smell like Sulphur, Sludge of course would smell like sewage and I guess Toxins would smell like drugs or chemicals. So, any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-02-2025, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T19:48:50-07:00","id":1554929,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles, I interpret Sense Wyrm more like a kind of sixth sense than something that affects one specific physical sense. It could manifest as your hair standing on end, goosebumps, sudden negative emotions, itching, headaches, runny nose, dry mouth, nausea, and so on. It could manifest as an olfactory hallucination, but it doesn't need to do so. Like how smelling something burning is sometimes a sign of a medical condition. Likewise it might manifest as some other sensory hallucination like spots before one's eyes, a ringing in the ear, and so on. However, I always make it clear that the character/player knows this is a result of sensing the Wyrm, not ordinary phenomenon.<br /> <br /> The difficulty of Sense Wyrm is supposed to be based on its concentration and strength, not a specific identification. So I never assigned a specific &quot;signal&quot; to a specific kind of Wyrm creature or effect. I don't think there's necessarily anything wrong with doing that. However, my preference is that Sense Wyrm should be used as something to get the PCs trying to figure out what caused it, rather than a solution that tells them exactly what it is they are facing. So while I do like the idea that maybe certain signals relate to certain kinds of Wyrm activity, I would want to avoid anything that clearly identifies the menace.<br /> <br /> I think Sense Wyrm works best as a prompt for the PCs. It confirms there is (or was) some kind of Wyrm taint in their immediate area, but they need to start using their other skills, powers, and noggin to figure out what it might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T07:54:29-08:00","id":1554959,"title":"","content":"Yeah, having to figure out where it is was also mentioned as a suggestion in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:36:21-08:00","id":1554968,"title":"","content":"But my point was that for example a girl named Becky is a fomor possessed by a Bane of Consumption, since Consumption is Entropy that particular branch of Wyrm-taint will smell like rotting flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  wording 11-02-2025, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T14:59:30-08:00","id":1554988,"title":"","content":"Disgusting. That's the one commonality between all the synesthetic hints of corruption that are usually presented in the writing. The 1994 Storyteller's Handbook has a list of potential &quot;Wyrmish&quot; qualities to scents on page 55, typically emphasizing rot or toxicity and sticking in the nose or mouth (barbed, crooked, hooked).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}